<title>USA: PaineWebber cuts bonds in portfolio - source.</title>
<headline>PaineWebber cuts bonds in portfolio - source.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>PaineWebber strategist Ed Kerschner has cut bond allocations by one percent in the firm's asset portfolio, according to a PaineWebber source.</p>
<p>The asset allocation model is now 37 percent bonds and 11 percent cash.  It was previously 38 percent bonds and 10 percent cash, the source said.</p>
<p>Stocks remained unchanged at 52 percent.</p>
</text>
